.TH GKNOWLEDGE-MCP 1 "October 2026" "gknowledge 0.3.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
gknowledge-mcp \- Model Context Protocol server for a gknowledge wiki
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B gknowledge-mcp
.RB [ \-\-init ]
.I PROJECT
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B gknowledge-mcp
lets Model Context Protocol clients, such as coding agents, use a
gknowledge project. It speaks JSON-RPC 2.0 over standard input and
output and offers the tools search_wiki, read_page, list_pages, ask,
add_source and recent_activity.
.PP
It is normally started by the MCP client, not by hand.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-init
Create
.I PROJECT
if it is not a gknowledge project yet. Without it, the server exits
when the folder is not a project.
.SH ARGUMENTS
.TP
.I PROJECT
Path to a gknowledge project folder.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B GKNOWLEDGE_PROJECT
Project path, used when
.I PROJECT
is not given.
.SH EXAMPLES
Register the server with Claude Code:
.PP
.nf
.RS
claude mcp add gknowledge \-\- gknowledge\-mcp ~/Knowledge/my\-project
.RE
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR gknowledge (1)
